<article class="env-remark" id="0G4N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0G4N">Remark <span data-tag="0G4N">48.30.5</span>.</a> Let $j : U \to X$ be an open immersion of Noetherian schemes. Sending $K \in D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ to a Deligne system whose restriction to $U$ is $K$ determines a functor </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  Rj_! : D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ U) \longrightarrow \text{Pro-}D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X)  \]
</div>
  <p> which is “exact” by Lemma <a href="/tag/0G4M" data-tag="0G4M">48.30.4</a> and which is “left adjoint” to the functor $j^* : D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ X) \to D^ b_{\textit{Coh}}(\mathcal{O}_ U)$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/0G2H" data-tag="0G2H">48.30.1</a>. </p>
</article>